extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 185-186 (cache p185-p186, page_offset 0); the people are introduced on 183-185, the R.C.C. stat block is printed 186. Printed 186 checked against a 110 dpi render, which agreed with the OCR on every number. || XP: the Larhold Barbarian / Neo-Human / Equinoid ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed. The book prints a ladder for the race, so it is stored; in a pairing the occupation''s ladder wins. || ATTRIBUTES as printed: I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 4D6+12 (supernatural), P.P. 3D6+2, P.E. 3D6+6, P.B. 2D4, Spd 3D4. || POOLS: M.D.C. P.E. plus 2D4x10, stored as mdc_base, so no men_of_arms line and no hit points. P.P.E. 3D6. Horror Factor 8 stored; the 10 where the reputation is known is conditional and is prose. || BONUSES stored: +1 attack per melee, +1 initiative, +2 roll with impact, +2 pull punch, +2 save vs magic (spell_magic), +6 vs horror factor. || PSIONICS: printed Standard, same as humans - no psionics block, so the race rolls on the standard table. MAGIC: none unless a magical O.C.C. is selected; the O.C.C. list is prose, not occ_restrictions, because the book says ''possible O.C.C.s include'' rather than limiting them. || SKILLS: Language: Larhold 98 (fixed; no literacy is printed). Language one of choice +15 as a Language: Other pick. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+10. Riding: War Bison 50+20 = 70 at 4 per level (catalog row from #1385: Horsemanship +10, the book''s own definition on this page). Wilderness Survival 30+15; Detect Ambush 30+10; Detect Concealment 25+10. W.P. Archery and Targeting is W.P. Archery; W.P. Sword; one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill each, no alignment condition printed. The book says that in addition to any O.C.C.''s skills every Larhold has Riding: War Bison and W.P. Archery; in a pairing the race''s whole R.C.C. skill list unions onto the O.C.C.''s, which grants more than that sentence names - recorded, not modelled. || RELATED: seven, plus two at level 3 and one at 6, 9 and 12. Communications, Espionage, Military, Pilot Related and W.P. any; Domestic +10; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Mechanical Automotive Mechanics only; Medical Holistic Medicine only +5; Physical +5 (where applicable - a skill with no percentage stays at zero); Pilot +5; Rogue +5; Technical +10; Wilderness +10; Science none. Horsemanship is not printed and not granted. SECONDARY: six, same limits without the bonuses. The book prints R.C.C. related and secondary lists for a race played on its own; in a pairing an occupation''s allowances replace them. || EQUIPMENT: larhold-composite-bow, larhold-saber and larhold-hide-armor are this book''s rows (#1392), which record the differing bow figures each class prints (+6 M.D. and P.S. 16 here). One energy weapon of choice and 1D4 E-clips; one modern weapon as a choice from a catalog set. The mount line is a War Bison OR a small vehicle: stored as a motorcycle choice, with the War Bison in the note because it is a creature (printed 187-188) with no gear row and is not stubbed. Camping kit as sleeping-bag, one week of dry rations as emergency-food-rations, cooking utensils as pot-metal (judgements). || MONEY: no Money line is printed; the Other Equipment line gives 1D6x1000 credits in cash or trade items, stored as 1d6x1000. In a pairing the race''s starting_money wins over the occupation''s, so a Larhold Shaman shows this figure rather than its own 2D6x1000."
