## Lore

The Larhold are a nomadic, horned humanoid people who came to Earth through
the Rifts of the Great Cataclysm. Their ancestors mastered a rare elemental
force, the Blue Flame, and learned to open dimensional gates, and whole tribes
have since roamed from world to world raiding, looting and enslaving. On Rifts
Earth their millions now range across the South American plains with herds of
cattle and packs of flesh-eating War Bison, forced south by the growing
nations to the north.

They look squat but stand about six feet tall, bow-legged from a life in the
saddle, with four small bison-like horns at the temples. Warriors favour cured
War Bison hide for armour and bows of bison bone and sinew so stiff only
supernatural arms can draw them, though wealthy raiders carry looted energy
weapons and ultra-tech armour.

Their danger lies less in their strength than in their tactics: ambushes,
feigned retreats, night raids and hostages used as living shields. They are
cruel even to one another and tribes war constantly, yet they cherish children
and often adopt the young of their enemies, which is why renegades of many
races ride among them.

## GM Notes

About 4.6 million live on the continent, 60% of them true Larhold. A tribe
holds 1,000 to 100,000 members and larger ones split into bands. Most tribes
answer to a chieftain and a shaman, and status is counted in "mounts".
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'larhold-barbarian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'larhold-barbarian';

